        <p>NOTlCE.—Solveri who become entitled to a prize in this competition can, if they desire, have any book on the game of Draughts equal to the value of ss. instead of cash prize, by notifying the Draughts Editor.</p>
        <p>In connection with the above competition we may state that we offsr a monthly prize of 5s to the competitor who succeeds in placing himself at the head of the Solvers' List at the end of the month. Where the prizs is, awarded the winner's score is cancelled, while the remaining competitors' points go towards the next month's zompetition. The win- ner may re-enter the c'impetition if he chooses commencing again at the bottom of the list. Points are awarded as follows: Two for the correct solu- tion of a problem, two for showing a dual 6olation, two for correcting the author's terms, and one for each minor correction. Intending competitors may commence at any time.</p>
