      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-12-01_WidnesExaminer_art0022" n="art0022">
        <head>N&amp;WS OF TI-10 GAME.</head>
        <p>N&amp;WS OF TI-10 GAME.</p>
        <p>BLINDFOLD PERFORMANCE BY WILLIE GA.RDNER. —On Tuesday evening last Willie Gardner, the English draughts and champion blindfold player of the world, gave an exhibition at the rooms of the Ilolbeck Liberal Club, Leed,,, playing blindfolded against tn opponents simultaneously. The Hol- beck Liberal Club had the services of a strong team, picked from the City club, to oppose the expert. Play commenced at eight o'clock in the presence of a large audience,and lasted until 10 45, when it was found the expert had scored five wins, one loss,and four draws. At various stages Gardner named the position or the pieces on the board, and called out the moves leading thereto. The tournament for the Liverpool championship has made very irregular progress, for while one player has reached the final, there are two still struggling in the second round. The unfinished heat in the first round between Collin and Cassin ended in favour of the first-named by 3 wins to 2 and I game drawn. Collin thus passed inco the st.cond round, but he immediately withdrew in favour of Nixon. Davies got a walk over from Cowie; Morrell beat Atherton by 4 games to 2. Cain and Jones hareonlv played three games, of which Cain won one and theothers were drawn. In the third round Nixon beat Davies 2 games to nil, and 3 draws. Nixon Otis enters the final. Morrell in the third round has to meet the winner in the heat between Cain and Junes. If Cain should win the heat, the real interest in the tournament will centre in his meeting with Morrell.</p>
