        <p>A else of considerable interest, in which a yoang lady Miss Eizaheth Watson, rtsiling at 237. South Alice- street, SJuth Shields, was concerned, has just he n re- ported. The incident has excited much comment in the neighbourhood. Miss Watson, a refined and intellilent younz ladq, appears to have had an eseape almost miraculous, and she good-natured allowed hersAi: to be interviewed by a " Seielda Daily News" represericative. Wnat she toll him sufficed to Wale the story •of her nar:ow escape beyond doubt. " Some sixteen months ago," she said, "I had the conam it) sfo-',..une to get my feet wet. I caught a chill and my hea!th was seriously aff?cte.d. Failing to shake off the eff etc of the efAA, I tee4ra3 very weak ad listlese,and completely Ins: all eojoyment in life. I was • placed u.lor the treat• meat of doe.tors, who after a .c ireful diagnosis pro- nounced me to be suffering from atcem'a. I vas almost bloodlesa, and the disease havin4 go: a firm ml I, tha doetors informed rne th.at Fowl mintns must elapse before rcc)4ary could 13:? eff,Mted. I was caTefully nursed, and.took their medicine faithfully, but my c on- (Sitio i st,erned t ) -he woe, mv in )ther and m.cs,df were at a loss to know woat to do. Evereu ally it was suggested that I should try Dr. William-i' pinA pills toe pale people, and I didso, with the' result that lam en- Orely cured, and feel better now than ever I dil in my Ufa." _ .</p>
        <p>Tais latt-r as3ertion was fully borne out by h appntrance. Askld how many b oxes she took to errec:: such a wonderful cure, she replied •"Seven." and added, with a feeling full of grateu le, that sae wig anxious that her case snoaid be made publie for the benefit of others similarly stricken. To U3e, he: own words: "I cannot express in vvorde how thankful lam for the goof the pills have dons me, and I shall recom- mend them. Illy greatest desire is that anyone suffering as I was may t eke Dr. Williams' pink pills, and [Otis safely say from experience that they will bs cured." In a. subst q sent interview with s,les Watson's mother, wino keeps as excellent grocery and pr ivision store at the address given above, the rep rter had this story eoe- finned in every p artienlar. Mrs. Watson, a lady very well known and most highly respected in the town, ex- pressed ti the representative her gratitu:te to Dr. Williams, whom she looks upon as the saviour of her chill's life. "My d auehter,''. she ex• plain° I. "is 18 rearm of age, and daring her illness she was entirely shut out from the pleasures of the world, and suffered p aroxystns of grief in c insequlnce. Everything was done for her ; but she lay like one half dfa.l, and her rec ivery seemed hop-less. 0.1 one occa- sion, in attempting to reach her place of employment, she f.. 11 in tne err ast through sheer exhaustion, and had to be brought back "lime." Asked how she cameto try Dr. Williams' pink pills fir pale peva,she said that she read of them ia the toe yspapers, and when everything else failed, she got a box of these pills as a last eh ince. Every dose was followed by perceptible ins- pr ivernent. At alert tin time:, and especially in the case cif ladies, wet feet may cause a great deal mire danger than might be anion ose.i. Cid at tie extremities of the body ent tila a waste of vital heat, and where the blood is poor. a slight wetting may -be toe culminating point of a threatened Mao:. Di. Williams' pink pills make new blood with every dese ; it will be nitea above that Mrs. Watson could actually trace in her daughter's case the beneicial eff ict of each dose as taken. A plentiful supply of geed and rich blood will ward off in any an illness, and the ii p lle are a safeguard agai ,st D!cembsr d angers for that reason. By their tonic and invigorating action they have cored mire than t wenty-tiv4 thousand cases of raeutna'isan, rheu- matic gout, sciatica, erz lora, S. Vitus' d•nce, fits, anm nia (or impaverislied btu yl), and .v-n C insumption, which often sacce de lane nit. Bu; subs itutes do not cure : the true pills are alwoys labelled w:th the fail name—Dr. Williams' pink pilts for pale peilple—andi may be had, if desire I—fr n Dr. Williams' Medicine Cunptny, Rol tarn Viadu ot, Load in. post free at two and ninepence a b ix—sic tntes thirteen and nine. is a got d p'au to o-d .1* then by Out ie substitution is attemp'ed by local snopicoapers.</p>
