      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-12-01_WidnesExaminer_art0102" n="art0102">
        <head>ALFRED WHITAKER.</head>
        <p>ALFRED WHITAKER.</p>
        <p>(From a</p>
        <p>The scientific world is still exper meriting with consumption, and is se arching for geese gpecili) to destroy the germs of disease, re3tore the w ei lung tissue, and finally bring the -body beck to a state of health. You have all no doubt read more or less about the ()c,nerese of Medical E cpteti at Berlie not long ago, for the express purws I ot ex- changing views about this terrible malady, Meanwhile, coneumption goes on making its in- roads into the health,attacking esi,eially the poorer classes of people, the majority of whom have yet to learn the most important lesson of all, which is ti prevent the development of the disease, and thus not be compelled to treat the disease itself. Is it not possible that scientific men are shooting over the heads of the very people whom they wish to penetrate with their scientific knowledge ? Is An not most important to point out to the people an easy and practical way te prevent the de- velopment of the disease? It is all very well to explain in the language of science, which few can understand, thet consumption is due to a vegetable life which finds a foothold in the lungs, and grows and multiplies there. But this is not especially satisfying when there follows the state- ment that nothing has yet been found to absolutely destroy this vegetable life. We think the truth re- vealed in the following letter will have more p:ac- tics' value te the people than the result of scientific discussion, which admits its inability to cure the disease under conseleration "Brickkiln Lane, Foleshill, Coventry, "February, 23:d, 1899. Gentlemen,—l am very pleavel indeed to tell you of the great good my boy has received from taking Scott'a Emulsion, and my only wish is that I had known of it ear-</p>
        <p>BOWLS. BOWLS. BOWLS BOWLING-GREEN BOWLS.</p>
        <p>JOSEPII DARLINGTON</p>
        <p>the noted old owl Turner, invites the inspection of his 00,1 selection of Bowls made out of the best quality dark lignum- vitce, and made at; idly to follow the jack. BILLIARD BALLS. ac.</p>
        <p>GENERAL WOOD AND IVORY TURNER.</p>
        <p>12, 14, &amp; 16, SLATER-STAEET, LIVERPOOL</p>
        <p>Established 1826.</p>
        <p>photograph.)</p>
        <p>her. I have lost two boys with consumption,. and tills one w.s going the same way, when hap- p,.niag to read of Scott's Emulsion and the great good it has done others, I tried it, and now, after taktng two bottles, my boy is a new child. In, fact our frieads are utterly surprised at the change in him in such a stiori-, time, as cn a.nd all were of the opinion that we should Iwo him. He had a nasty hacking cough, getting no rest day or night from it. Ele could hardly talc., any food at all, and what he did take did him no good. He was getting so weak and thin that he could hardly stand. He is now quite well, eats all before him and is getting as fat now as he was getting thin before. He is so fond of Scott's Emukion t,oat we have a job to make him satisfleJ with his dose, which is a grand thing as medicine is generally a difficult thing to get children to take. I have pleasure in enclosing his photo, arid shall always recommend Scott's E*3111.• sion wherever I can, as lam sure it has saved his life and made him what he is —Yours wry truly. (Signed) (llrs.).A. Wrarraxma." We cannot for a moment put ourselves above science. because Scott's Emulsion is in itself a scientific preparation, but it is our endeav,ur above all things to be practical, and by pointing out the practical results from taking Slott's Emulsion we think we are doing a great deal to prevent the development of consumption. Consumption attacks the weak; the strong resist it. We believe science will admir this principle.as it also admits the superior merits of Scott's Emulsion.</p>
        <p>You can obtain a sample of Scott'a Emulsion by sending tlareepence to cover postage to Scott and Bowne, Limited, Manufacturing Chemisrs, 95,Great Saffron Hill, London, EC., and mentioning this paper. All chemists s,tli Scott's Emn'sion.</p>
