        <p>Lady Married s a lady marred. So the old proverb :runs, but ir, plain Anglo-Suron " It's a lie." If thc lady le, marred thrmigh marriage, we know where to lay the blame. It is net all Jill's fault, Jack has the larger share in the marring. S Aomon says " An odious woman when she is married " is oce of the things for which " the earth is disquieted, and cannot bear," but the majnity of ladies we have met are not odious, but odorous, and very sweetly so. The best society in the world is a pure, sweet, noble-minded woman. A lady's health may be marred through Indige3tion, Wind on the Stomach, Liver Complaints, Sick Headache, Costiveness, Nervous Deti!ity, Palpitation of the Heart, Bilious- ness, Sze., but Page Woodcock's Wind Pills are a sovereign remedy, and ought to be used imme- diately.</p>
        <p>Mr. Gxrge Wright, Agent for the " Prudential," 12, Weumau-street, Birmingham, writes :—" Your Wind Pills have done me an immense amount of good. I suffered severely from Wind and Colic in the 13c,wels. My wife advised me to try your Wind Pills. Result—Good health and lasting grati- tude to you. I recommend yotlr Wind Pills every •</p>
        <p>1 4.9g1.1t1221.0. Ivroto the Proprietor of Page Wood- cc's Wind Pills a few days ago E taring thac fur a 0 fiver Ile ifOUld send him and alio 7, him t) uee a 1 b ena-fide testini6nigi to his Wird Pi,le, Page Wocd- cock replied he Lever had F. n d never wou:d buy testimolials. He gets scores from grateful patients, wbo gladly allow him to use their names.</p>
        <p>Page Woodcock's Wind Tills being purely Vege- table, Tasteless, and Mild and Tonic in their action, may be taken with patient safety by the most deli- cate of either sex. Children may safely take them in reduced doses. Page Woodcock's Wind Pills are sold by. all Medicine Vendors at is. lid. and Bs. 9d, ; post free or price by Page Woodcock, Lincoln.</p>
