        <p>* "WARRINGTON EXAMI Each Club is numbered lor 2. All the Competitor has to do space provided. If a draw is intended put X. -NOTE —Don't cut the Coupon into strips, send the complete form. This Competition is run in conjunction with the " o,ampetition Key," and,othec papers. NAME ADDRESS CONDITIONS. I.—The first coupon is free, and no competitor can sand in more then one free coupon. Enclose Id. stamp for every other coupon used. One Shitli g Postal Order must be enclose lif all toe nitipotie on above sheet are used Any number of coup ma van be sent in if paid for at the rate of One Shilling for each 20. 2.—Cross all Postal Orders and keep the numbers. 3.—No competitor can take more than one share of tie £lO prize. 4.—The coupons must be forwarded to the Sxaminer ORITI Warrington, the envelope to 4e endorsed Football Coupon," BO as to be delivered by the first post on Thursday morning. If the envelope bears Wednesday's postmark, it will be received up to 5 p.m. on Thursday. Coupons delivered by hand must be received not later than 9 a.m. on Thursday. 5.—Competitors demanding a scrutiny must enclose fee of Ten Shillings, give number of Postal Or r (if any), and num- ber of coupons sent. In the event of the claim proving correct the fe will be returned. 6.—lnthe event of two or more competitors tying, prize money will be divided. • 7.—A1l attempts in this competition must be made on coupons cut from this paper. B.—When not less than 40 attempts are made, the coupons of unsuceessful competitors for the coupon prize will be carried forward and added to the number sent in, in the next competition,so that sooner or later the coupon prize must be won by regular competitors • 9.—The results will appear in the first issue following the result of the matches. [RESULTS OF COMPETITI )N AND LIST OF WINNERS ON PAGE 5.]</p>
